          <div class="company-experience-group">
            <article class="details-container experience-role">
              <header class="role-header">
                <div class="role-identity">
                  <h3 class="role-title">Machine Learning Research Assistant</h3>
                  <p class="role-company">Texas A&amp;M University</p>
                </div>
                <div class="role-meta">
                  <time class="role-dates">Nov 2024 - Dec 2025</time>
                  <span class="role-location">College Station, TX</span>
                </div>
              </header>
              <p class="role-summary">
                Biomedical machine learning research on pulmonary blood-flow modeling
                and medical imaging.
              </p>
              <ul class="experience-bullets">
                <li class="experience-bullet">
                  Developed a transformer model that estimates pulmonary artery blood
                  pressure across 200+ patient vessel models without an invasive
                  procedure, producing results accepted at ASME SB3C 2025, by training
                  on 3D vessel geometry and boundary conditions to an R² of 0.95.
                </li>
                <li class="experience-bullet">
                  Trained a U-Net model that segments 500+ CT scans into 3D pulmonary
                  artery reconstructions, saving 2 weeks of manual anatomy prep per
                  patient case, by automating segmentation ahead of blood-flow
                  simulation.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </article>

            <div
              class="company-metrics"
              data-company="Texas A&amp;M University"
              aria-label="Texas A&amp;M University outcomes"
            >
              <div class="metric-tile">
                <strong>200+</strong>
                <span>patient vessel models</span>
              </div>
              <div class="metric-tile">
                <strong>2 weeks</strong>
                <span>of manual prep saved per patient case</span>
              </div>
              <div class="metric-tile">
                <strong>Accepted</strong>
                <span>at ASME SB3C 2025</span>
              </div>
            </div>
